    <statement><p>Use difference quotients with <m>\Delta x = 0.1</m> and
<m>\Delta y = 0.1</m> to estimate <m>f_x(2,4)</m> and
<m>f_y(2,4)</m> where
<me>f(x,y) = e^{-x}\sin\mathopen{}\left(y\right).</me></p>
<p><m>f_x(2,4) \approx</m> <fillin characters="25" name="AnSwEr0001"/></p>
<p><m>f_y(2,4) \approx</m> <fillin characters="25" name="AnSwEr0002"/></p>
<p>Then give better estimates by using <m>\Delta x = 0.01</m> and
<m>\Delta y = 0.01</m>.</p>
<p><m>f_x(2,4) \approx</m> <fillin characters="25" name="AnSwEr0003"/></p>
<p><m>f_y(2,4) \approx</m> <fillin characters="25" name="AnSwEr0004"/></p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>0.0974675</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>-0.0831968</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>0.101912</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>-0.0879475</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <solution><m>\Delta x=0.1</m> and <m>\Delta y =0.1</m>, we have the estimates:
<me>f_x(2,4) \approx \frac{f(2.1,4) - f(2,4)}{0.1}
         = \frac{e^{-2.1}\,\sin(4) - e^{-2}\,\sin(4)}{0.1}
         \approx \frac{-0.0926753  + 0.102422}{0.1} = 0.0974675.</me>
and
<me>f_y(2,4) \approx \frac{f(2,4.1) - f(2,4)}{0.1}
	= \frac{e^{-2}\,\sin(4.1) - e^{-2}\,\sin(4)}{0.1}
        \approx \frac{-0.110742  + 0.102422}{0.1} = -0.0831968.</me>
Now, using <m>\Delta x=0.01</m> and <m>\Delta y=0.01</m>, we have the estimates:
<me>f_x(2,4) \approx \frac{f(2.01,4) - f(2,4)}{0.01}
        = \frac{e^{-2.01}\,\sin(4) - e^{-2}\,\sin(4)}{0.01}
        \approx \frac{-0.101403  + 0.102422}{0.01} = 0.101912</me>
and
<me>f_x(2,4) \approx \frac{f(2,4.01) - f(2,4)}{0.01}
        = \frac{e^{-2}\,\sin(4.01) - e^{-2}\,\sin(4)}{0.01}
        \approx \frac{-0.103302  + 0.102422}{0.01} = -0.0879475.</me>



</solution>
